APIS">3819</idno><note type="comment">According to [4LDAV8UH]: 96, his dates are probably 1084-1171 as he is reported to have been born in a rat year, and to have had a long life (88, 99, or 100 years).</note></person><person xml:id="person3917"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཆོས་གྲགས</persName><birth notBefore="1140-01-01">after 1140</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P0RK976</idno><idno type="APIS">3917</idno></person><person xml:id="person8623"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sugataśrī</persName><birth notAfter="1117-12-31">before 1117</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="APIS">8623</idno><note type="comment">Identical with (ID:6616)?</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3692"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">aṣṭasāhasrikāprajñāpāramitā</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'phags pa shes rab kyi pha rol tu phyin pa brgyad stong pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ārya-aṣṭasāhasrikā-prajñāpāramitā</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgyal ba'i yum bsdus pa brgyad stong pa</title><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Prajñāpāramitā sutra in 8000 verses.</note><idno type="APIS">3692</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work4637"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgyal ba'i yum bsdus pa brgyad stong pa'i rnam par bshad pa</title><title xml:lang="bo">རྒྱལ་བའི་ཡུམ་བསྡུས་པ་བརྒྱད་སྟོང་པའི་རྣམ་པར་བཤད་པ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shAkya'i dge slong chos grags kyis mdzad pa'i rgyal ba'i yum bsdus pa brgyad stong pa'i rnam par bshad pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgyal yum bsdus pa'i rnam bshad</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><author ref="person:3917">chos grags</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">In the verse of intention in the incipit, the work is presented as setting forth the meaning of the rGyal yum bsdus pa. The lemmata indicate a commentary on Aṣṭasāhasrikāprajñāpāramitā (ID:3692).&#13;
&#13;
References are made to the interpretation of Haribhadra (ID:3712) and the 'Bum tig (ID:8586).&#13;
&#13;
The author cites the views of rNgog Blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786), 'Bre (ID:3807), Ar (ID:3816), La stod pa (ID:3819), su ga ta shri, and - using the honorific "gsung" - of an unidentified "teacher" (slob dpon). &#13;
Satyadvayāvatāra (ID:6060) is cited as well.</note><relatedItem type="commentaryOn" target="work:3692"/><idno type="APIS">4637</idno></bibl></listBibl><listRelation><relation xml:id="rel8213" name="quotes-with-name" active="#person3917" passive="#person3816" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex022052026-11-0510-22-03"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel8212" name="quotes-with-name" active="#person3917" passive="#person3807" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex022052026-11-0510-22-02"/><ptr target="#ex022052026-11-0510-22-03"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel8215" name="quotes-with-name" active="#person3917" passive="#person8623" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex022052026-11-0511-03-41"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel8211" name="quotes-with-name" active="#person3917" passive="#person3786" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex022052026-11-0510-22-01"/><ptr target="#ex022052026-11-0510-22-02"/><ptr target="#ex022052026-11-0510-22-04"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel666" name="author-of" active="#person3917" passive="#work4637" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex22052024-10-1809-27-10"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel8214" name="quotes-with-name" active="#person3917" passive="#person3819" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex022052026-11-0510-39-56"/></desc></relation></listRelation></standOff><text>
